<title>JAPAN: Japan Aug beef imports fall 29.5 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Aug beef imports fall 29.5 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in August were down 29.5 percent from a year earlier, according to data released by the Finance Ministry on Monday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   August 96     July 96    August 95</p>
<p> Total	    42,444	 74,567	60,232</p>
<p> Refrigerated   25,938	 26,939	34,919</p>
<p> Frozen	   16,506	 47,628	25,314</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):   Australia     15,003	 16,216	20,722</p>
<p>  U.S.	    10,245	  9,965	13,108</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		  August 96    July 96     August 95</p>
<p> U.S.	     9,027	 28,727	15,979</p>
<p> Australia	6,002	 15,632	 6,581</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first eight months of 1996 were 220,052 tonnes, against 226,333 tonnes during the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the first eight months of 1996 came to 239,498 tonnes, against 187,459 tonnes in the same period of 1995.</p>
